---
description: Committed TypeScript must not import files listed in .gitignore
globs: app/**/*.{ts,tsx},lib/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# No gitignored imports from committed code

A clean clone cannot `next build` if tracked routes or libs import `.ts` that `.gitignore` excludes. That already happened: Insights routes and `lib/auth/require-admin.ts` imported `lib/insights/access.ts` (and related modules) while those files were ignored.

**Do**

- Before adding an import, check `.gitignore`. If the target is ignored, do not import it from a committed file.
- Either commit the module (when it is not secret) or stop importing it from tracked code.
- Keep Insights harness (`lib/insights/harness/`) local-only; do not wire it from tracked routes.

**Do not**

- Add new `app/api/**` or `lib/**` imports of gitignored TypeScript.
- Assume a file that exists only on this machine will exist for every clone.
